        <h2><strong>Commercial Aerosol Production</strong></h2>
        <p>Commercial production focuses on consistent large-scale manufacturing while maintaining cost efficiency,
            quality standards, and regulatory compliance. In standard aerosol production lines, valves are inserted and
            crimped before propellant filling, except in specific under-the-cup gassing systems. This operational
            sequence is critical for ensuring filling accuracy and hardware compatibility.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Automated filling and gassing lines</li>
            <li>High-speed valve insertion and crimping</li>
            <li>Pressure testing and leakage verification</li>
            <li>Vendor-approved raw materials and hardware</li>
        </ul>

        <h3><strong>Typical Commercial Scale Batch Sizes</strong></h3>
        <ul>
            <li>1–10 tons concentrate</li>
            <li>10,000–200,000 cans per shift depending on line speed</li>
        </ul>

        <h3><strong>Regulatory Load</strong></h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Full QA/QC protocols for every batch</li>
            <li>BIS/ISO requirements; GMP applies only to pharmaceutical or regulated cosmetic aerosols</li>
            <li>Pressure and leakage testing compliance</li>
            <li>Propellant safety and hazardous-area certification</li>
        </ul>

